    (\u042d\u043c\u0438\u043b\u044c \u0410\u0440\u0442\u0438\u043d, 1927) | \u0413\u0438\u043b\u044c\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0442
    \u043d\u0435 \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0441\u0442\u043e \u0441\u0442\u0430\u0432\u0438\u043b \u0437\u0430\u0434\u0430\u0447\u0438
    \u2014 \u043e\u043d \u0432\u0441\u0435\u043b\u044f\u043b \u0432 \u043c\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043c\u0430\u0442\u0438\u043a\u043e\u0432
    \u0432\u0435\u0440\u0443 \u0432 \u043c\u043e\u0433\u0443\u0449\u0435\u0441\u0442\u0432\u043e
    \u0438\u0445 \u043d\u0430\u0443\u043a\u0438. \u0415\u0433\u043e \u0437\u043d\u0430\u043c\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0442\u044b\u0439
    \u0434\u0435\u0432\u0438\u0437, \u0432\u044b\u0441\u0435\u0447\u0435\u043d\u043d\u044b\u0439
    \u043d\u0430 \u043c\u043e\u0433\u0438\u043b\u0435, \u00abWir m\u00fcssen wissen. Wir werden
    wissen\u00bb (\u00ab\u041c\u044b \u0434\u043e\u043b\u0436\u043d\u044b \u0437\u043d\u0430\u0442\u044c.
    \u041c\u044b \u0431\u0443\u0434\u0435\u043c \u0437\u043d\u0430\u0442\u044c\u00bb), \u0441\u0442\u0430\u043b
    \u0441\u0438\u043c\u0432\u043e\u043b\u043e\u043c \u0435\u0433\u043e \u043d\u0435\u0441\u0433\u0438\u0431\u0430\u0435\u043c\u043e\u0433\u043e
    \u043e\u043f\u0442\u0438\u043c\u0438\u0437\u043c\u0430 \u0438 \u0432\u0435\u0440\u044b \u0432
    \u0441\u0438\u043b\u0443 \u0447\u0435\u043b\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0447\u0435\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0433\u043e
    \u0440\u0430\u0437\u0443\u043c\u0430."
  achievementsEn: "Of course, David Gilbert's contribution to science is so extensive and profound that he is rightly regarded as one of the last great universal mathematicians, and he has not merely solved complex problems; he has created whole directions, re-thinking the basis of the disciplines, and determining the ways in which mathematics can be developed for decades to come; his legacy can be traced from abstract algebra to quantum physics.Here is a detailed overview of its major achievements, organized by science.\n\nIn 1899, Gilbert published his work \"Grundlagen der Geometrie\", which revolutionized the understanding of geometry and the whole mathematical method.For Gilbert, axioms are not obvious truths, but implicit definitions, the formal conditions imposed on these concepts, which meant that instead of \"point is that it has no parts\", he used axiom \"through any two points one straight line can be made.\" Completeness and consistency: Gilbert gave the complete system axiom of euclidic geometry and, equally important, strict proof of their consistency and independence from each other.To that end, he built a series of witty models (e.g., arithmetical models) showing that one axiom could not be taken out of the others.\n\nInvariant theory and algebraic numbers The beginning of Gilbert's scientific path was devoted to the theory of invariants, an area that explores the properties of algebraic forms that do not change in linear changes. The theory of the limb of the base: His main achievement here was proof of the \"main theorem\" of the existence of an end base for any system of invariants.This evidence was revolutionary, but not constructive: it claimed existence, but did not give the algorithm to find it; this led to criticism by Paul Gordan's senior colleague, who said, \"It's not mathematics, it's theology!\" but later he recognized the significance of the result.The \"Number Report\" (Zahlberich): In 1897, he published a monumental survey on algebraic numbers theory, which systematized all knowledge of the subject at the time and became a fundamental work for many years.\n\n==Early life==In the early 20th century, Gilbert introduced the theory of integrated equations. The result of his work was the creation of a new section of mathematics, functional analysis. The birth of Gilbert Space: Working with integrated equations, he introduced the notion of infinite space where the points are functions and distance is determined by integral.This space, later named Gilbertian, became the basis for all modern mathematical physics and quantum mechanics. Spectrum theory: It developed a spectrum theory for compact operators in the Gilbert space, which allows, for example, to find \"own values\" and \"own functions\" for complex mathematical objects.The solution to Varing's problem: In Gilbert's theory, the problem of Varing has been brilliantly demonstrated that for any natural `n' there is such a number `g(n)' that any whole positive number can be presented as the sum of no more than `g(n)' of the sum, each of which is `n' the second degree of the number.\n\nGilbert's math physicist thought that physics, like geometry, should be built on a strict axiomatic basis. The theory of relativity: His interest in physics was not abstract. During Albert Einstein's work on the general theory of relativity, Gilbert advised him and assisted in the development of a mathematical machine, a four-dimensional test.Axiomatization of physics: He actively called for the axiomaticization of all physics, as reflected in his famous sixth issue. Although the complete axiomaticization of all physics has not yet been completed, his call was inspired by the creation of axiomatic bases for thermodynamics, a special theory of relativity, and later quantum mechanics (John von Neyman) and probability theory (Andray Kolmogorov).\n\nIn the 1920s, Gilbert's mathematics philosophy and Gilbert's programme, the most ambitious, though ultimately unsuccessful, was to protect all mathematics from internal contradictions. In the 1920s, he developed his famous program. The program's goal is to prove that math is inconsistible. To this end, he suggested: 1. Formalize all mathematics into a game with symbols according to strict rules (formal system).By means of \"final\" (final and visual) meta-thematic methods, it is impossible to prove in this formal system that the claim and its denial could not be simultaneously taken out. In 1931, Kurt Goedel's young logic published its theories of incompleteness, which caused a devastating blow to Gilbert's program.Godel showed that in any fairly complex system, including arithmetic, there are allegations that can neither be proved nor denied in this system. Consequently, it is impossible to prove its consistency by its own means. Unexpected results: Although the primary goal was not achievable, Gilbert's own program has given rise to the theory of evidence, the theory of algorithms and all modern mathematical logic.\n\nHe presented a list of 23 outstanding issues that he believed would determine the development of mathematics for the twentieth century, which became the \"track map\" for mathematicians around the world.Here are just some of the most famous problems and their fate: the problem of the problem is the specific description of the status of the solution. :----------------------------------------1-- 1-Continuum-hypothesis of Cantor ♪ has been shown to be independent of the axiom of multiple theory (Gödel, Cohen, 1940-1963) ♪2 ♪ Arifmetics Inconsistency ♪ It's shown that it's impossible to prove by the arithmetic itself (Gödel, 1931) ~ The equality of multi-dimensionals is not the answer (Max Dan, op. cit.(190) ♪ Axiomatization of physics ♪ axiomatization of physics ♪ the solution (probability theory, mechanics, quantum mechanics) ♪ 7 ♪ Transcendence of species number a♪b ♪ is the answer ♪ (Theorm of Helfand-Snyder, 1934) ♪ 8 ♪ Riman's hypothesis ♪ Unsolved (one of the main problems of modern mathematics) ♪ 10 ♪ The tolerance of diofant equations ♪ is the answer to the problem (Juria Matiacevic, J.1970) ♪ 17 ♪ The presentation of positive functions by the sum of squares ♪ isn't just a challenge -- he gave mathematicians the faith in their science. His famous motto, written on the grave, \"Wir müssen wissen. Weir Werden wissen\" (\"We must know, we will know\"), became a symbol of his unflagging optimism and faith in the power of the human mind."
  personalLifeRu: "\u041b\u0438\u0447\u043d\u0430\u044f \u0436\u0438\u0437\u043d\u044c \u0414\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0434\u0430
    \u0413\u0438\u043b\u044c\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0442\u0430, \u0432 \u043e\u0442\u043b\u0438\u0447\u0438\u0435
    \u043e\u0442 \u0435\u0433\u043e \u043f\u0443\u0431\u043b\u0438\u0447\u043d\u044b\u0445 \u0442\u0440\u0438\u0443\u043c\u0444\u043e\u0432,
    \u0431\u044b\u043b\u0430 \u043d\u0430\u043f\u043e\u043b\u043d\u0435\u043d\u0430 \u043a\u0430\u043a
    \u0433\u043b\u0443\u0431\u043e\u043a\u043e\u0439 \u043f\u0440\u0438\u0432\u044f\u0437\u0430\u043d\u043d\u043e\u0441\u0442\u044c\u044e
    \u0438 \u0434\u0440\u0443\u0436\u0431\u043e\u0439, \u0442\u0430\u043a \u0438 \u0442\u0440\u0430\u0433\u0435\u0434\u0438\u0435\u0439,
    \u043a\u043e\u0442\u043e\u0440\u0443\u044e \u043e\u043d \u0438 \u0435\u0433\u043e \u0441\u0435\u043c\u044c\u044f
    \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0436\u0438\u0432\u0430\u043b\u0438 \u0432 \u0442\u0435\u043d\u0438
    \u0435\u0433\u043e \u0433\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0434\u0438\u043e\u0437\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u043d\u0430\u0443\u0447\u043d\u043e\u0439
    \u043a\u0430\u0440\u044c\u0435\u0440\u044b.\n\n\U0001F491 \u0411\u0440\u0430\u043a \u0441
    \u041a\u0435\u0442\u0435 \u0415\u0440\u043e\u0448 \u0412 1892 \u0433\u043e\u0434\u0443 \u0413\u0438\u043b\u044c\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0442
    \u0436\u0435\u043d\u0438\u043b\u0441\u044f \u043d\u0430 \u041a\u0435\u0442\u0435 \u0415\u0440\u043e\u0448
    (K\u00e4the Jerosch, 1864\u20131945). \u041e\u043d\u0430 \u0431\u044b\u043b\u0430 \u0434\u043e\u0447\u0435\u0440\u044c\u044e
    \u043a\u0451\u043d\u0438\u0433\u0441\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0433\u0441\u043a\u043e\u0433\u043e
    \u0442\u043e\u0440\u0433\u043e\u0432\u0446\u0430 \u0438, \u043f\u043e \u043e\u043f\u0438\u0441\u0430\u043d\u0438\u044f\u043c,
    \u043e\u0442\u043b\u0438\u0447\u0430\u043b\u0430\u0441\u044c \u043f\u0440\u044f\u043c\u043e\u0442\u043e\u0439
    \u0438 \u043d\u0435\u0437\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0441\u0438\u043c\u043e\u0441\u0442\u044c\u044e
    \u0443\u043c\u0430, \u0447\u0442\u043e \u043e\u0447\u0435\u043d\u044c \u0441\u043e\u043e\u0442\u0432\u0435\u0442\u0441\u0442\u0432\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043b\u043e
    \u0445\u0430\u0440\u0430\u043a\u0442\u0435\u0440\u0443 \u0441\u0430\u043c\u043e\u0433\u043e
    \u0413\u0438\u043b\u044c\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0442\u0430. \u0418\u0445 \u0431\u0440\u0430\u043a
    \u0441\u0442\u0430\u043b \u043a\u0440\u0435\u043f\u043a\u0438\u043c \u0441\u043e\u044e\u0437\u043e\u043c,
    \u0438 \u041a\u0435\u0442\u0435 \u043d\u0430 \u043f\u0440\u043e\u0442\u044f\u0436\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0438
    \u0432\u0441\u0435\u0439 \u0436\u0438\u0437\u043d\u0438 \u043e\u0441\u0442\u0430\u0432\u0430\u043b\u0430\u0441\u044c
    \u0435\u0433\u043e \u0432\u0435\u0440\u043d\u043e\u0439 \u0441\u043f\u0443\u0442\u043d\u0438\u0446\u0435\u0439.
    \u0412 1893 \u0433\u043e\u0434\u0443 \u0443 \u043d\u0438\u0445 \u0440\u043e\u0434\u0438\u043b\u0441\u044f
    \u0435\u0434\u0438\u043d\u0441\u0442\u0432\u0435\u043d\u043d\u044b\u0439 \u0441\u044b\u043d
    \u0424\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0446.\n\n\U0001F468\u200d\U0001F466 \u041e\u0442\u0446\u043e\u0432\u0441\u0442\u0432\u043e
    \u0438 \u0441\u0435\u043c\u0435\u0439\u043d\u0430\u044f \u0442\u0440\u0430\u0433\u0435\u0434\u0438\u044f
